"libdriver.so\");\n    p\n}\n\n/// Capture everything written to stdout during the closure by replacing\n/// fd 1 with a pipe. Returns the raw bytes.\nfn capture_stdout<F: FnOnce()>(f: F) -> Vec<u8> {\n    use std::os::unix::io::AsRawFd;\n    // Flush Rust's stdout buffer first\n    use std::io::Write;\n    let _ = std::io::stdout().flush();\n\n    // Create a pipe\n    let mut fds = [0 as libc::c_int; 2];\n    let rc = unsafe { libc::pipe(fds.as_mut_ptr()) };\n    assert_eq!(rc, 0, \"pipe() failed\");\n    let read_fd: RawFd = fds[0];\n    let write_fd: RawFd = fds[1];\n\n    // Save the current stdout and dup the pipe write end onto fd 1\n    let saved_stdout: RawFd = unsafe { libc::dup(1) };\n    assert!(saved_stdout >= 0, \"dup(1) failed\");\n    let rc = unsafe { libc::dup2(write_fd, 1) };\n    assert!(rc >= 0, \"dup2 failed\");\n    unsafe { libc::close(write_fd) };\n\n    // Run the function\n    f();\n\n    // Flush libc stdout\n    unsafe {\n        let _ = libc::fflush(std::ptr::null_mut());\n    }\n\n    // Restore original stdout\n    let rc = unsafe { libc::dup2(saved_stdout, 1) };\n    assert!(rc >= 0, \"dup2 restore failed\");\n    unsafe { libc::close(saved_stdout) };\n\n    // Read everything from the pipe\n    let mut file = unsafe { std::fs::File::from_raw_fd(read_fd) };\n    let mut out = Vec::new();\n    // Set non-blocking? We've already closed the write fd in this process;\n    // however the dup2'd copy was on fd 1 which we restored. So the only\n    // remaining write end was the dup2 copy on fd 1, which is now gone.\n    file.read_to_end(&mut out).expect(\"read pipe\");\n    let _ = file.into_raw_fd(); // ensure fd is closed via Drop of File at end of scope; into_raw_fd skips that. Use drop instead:\n    // Actually we want File to close on drop. Re-wrap:\n    out\n}\n\nextern crate libc;\n\n// Function signature types\ntype FnPrintLine = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char);\ntype FnPrintIntLine = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(c_int);\ntype FnBa